cost_model:
Measured (G4 R22, same code; per-order counts from C's sidecar on the same input 0baa4de1, whose sums equal R22 tower_work). A(K) on 08/000000 costs about 180-190 ns per block (about 700 cycles) and 107-124 ns per facet for K2..K5, and 250-290 ns per node on all six frames at K5. It rises to 300-370 ns/node in K10 runs. K10 order 10: 279 ns/block, 154 ns/facet, 360 ns/node. The same order 2 (identical program and blocks) costs 287 ns/node in the K5 run and 356 in the K10 run (1.31 M vs 5.51 M balls, plus more runners): BallId-indexed and O(balls) structures, and contention, cost measurably. A(1) (699 ns/block) is inflated by the sequential K1 loop and by running inside phase 0 (43-59 ms in R17-R20, 69-82 ms in R21-R22 at K5).

Fixed per order (K5 order 5 / K10 order 10), a few ms in total, about 3-5 % of A(K):
- anchors.assign of 4·|balls| B (5.2 / 22.1 MB), single-threaded, first touch;
- lean arrays of 7·M B, zero-filled then rewritten, plus up to 48 threads created per order by a runner that does not own the pool (R22 helper_threads 409 at K5, 889 at K10);
- the O(N) live scan.

So the per-block loop is at least 90 % of A(K). Per block at K5: F/M = 1.71 facets, 2.74 compressed hops and 2.0 path writes per facet, and at most 0.73 published batches. That is about 13.6 random cache-line touches:
- catalogue 224-B records, about 1.7 lines (n_shell/arity at 1244 + lot level at 1378/1297);
- level_run about 2.7 (1380, 1267);
- anchors about 2.7 (1268-1269 reads + 1301/1350 write);
- compressed about 4.7 dependent hops (1152);
- next about 1.7 (1156).

The dependent chain per facet is anchors → compressed x2.7 → next, about 4.7 loads. The random working set excluding the catalogue is 19.7 MB at K5 order 5 and 70.3 MB at K10 order 10. G4 has an EPYC 9B45: 1 MB L2 per core, 32 MB L3 per CCD, THP state unknown.

Grouped lots allocate about 7 + 3·groups malloc/free each (26,301 lots at K5, 33,221 at K2, 18,232 at K1); singleton lots allocate nothing. First-touch writes are about 76 MB (18.6 k pages) at K5 order 5 and about 223 MB (54 k pages) at K10 order 10, about 1.2 GB over the K10 orders. The 48-B ExactLevel per batch alone is up to 27.7 / 78.7 MB.

Model, to be fitted on rdtsc sub-timers, minflt and zero-risk ablations: T_A(K) = T_fix + M·c_blk + F·c_fct + G·c_grp + N·c_node + P·c_page. Plausible attribution (projection):
- about 8 L3-latency dependent loads per block ≈ 400 cycles;
- partly overlapped catalogue misses ≈ 100-300 cycles;
- page faults 5-13 %;
- grouped-lot allocations 5-15 % at K1-K3, 3-6 % at K5.

Caveat: C's physical-head ablation cut hops without any gain, so the chains are not the only cost.

Window impact (recomputed from R22): dividing all A(K) by 2 or 4 takes 00/K5 from 186 ms to 116 / 97 ms, and b02/K5 from 432 to 250 / 196 ms. At K10 the window stays capped by phase 0: 893 → 782 / 756, and 391 only with phase 0 ÷2 as well.
